<title>GERMANY: SWIMMING-ROLPH EQUALS EUROPEAN 200 MEDLEY RECORD.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-ROLPH EQUALS EUROPEAN 200 MEDLEY RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>ROSTOCK, Germany 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Susan Rolph of Britain equalled the European record in the women's short-course 200 metres medley on Sunday.</p>
<p>Rolph clocked two minutes 10.60 seconds at the European sprints and short-course swimming championships to equal the mark set by East German Petra Schneider in Gainesville, Florida, on January 8, 1982.</p>
